<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Defs>

    <FactionDef ParentName="FactionBase">
        <defName>ESCP_Faction_Stormcloaks</defName>
        <label>Stormcloak Rebellion</label>
        <description>The Stormcloaks are the rebel army of Ulfric Stormcloak, Jarl of Windhelm, fighting to drive the Imperial Legion from Skyrim and reclaim the province's right to govern itself. Their cause is bound up with the Talos question, the White-Gold Concordat that ended the Great War banned the worship of Tiber Septim as a god, something the Nords of Skyrim refused to accept. Ulfric killed the High King with the Voice and claimed the throne was his by right of trial by combat. The Empire calls it murder. The Stormcloaks call it justice. Their army is less disciplined than the Legion's but fights on its own soil with the kind of ferocity that comes from defending something personal.</description>
        <colorSpectrum>
            <li>(0.15, 0.22, 0.55)</li>
        </colorSpectrum>
        <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>0</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
        <pawnSingular>Stormcloak</pawnSingular>
        <pawnsPlural>Stormcloaks</pawnsPlural>
        <categoryTag>Outlander</categoryTag>
        <settlementGenerationWeight>0.25</settlementGenerationWeight>
        <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
        <canSiege>true</canSiege>
        <canStageAttacks>true</canStageAttacks>
        <leaderTitle>Jarl</leaderTitle>
        <factionIconPath>World/WorldObjects/Expanding/Empire</factionIconPath>
        <techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
        <fixedName>Stormcloak Rebellion</fixedName>
        <allowedCultures>
            <li>ESCP_Culture_Nord</li>
        </allowedCultures>

        <royalTitleTags>
            <li>ESCP_Title_Stormcloak</li>
        </royalTitleTags>
        <royalFavorLabel>Loyalty to Skyrim</royalFavorLabel>
        <royalTitleInheritanceWorkerClass>RoyalTitleInheritanceWorker</royalTitleInheritanceWorkerClass>

        <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
        <ideoName>Nine Divines</ideoName>
        <ideoDescription>The Nine Divines are the divine pantheon of the Cyrodiilic Empire: Akatosh, Arkay, Dibella, Julianos, Kynareth, Mara, Stendarr, Zenithar, and Talos. The Stormcloaks worship all nine openly. Talos is not an addendum to their faith; he is the reason they are fighting. The White-Gold Concordat banned his veneration and gave the Thalmor legal authority to arrest worshippers. Every Stormcloak who lights a candle in his name does so as an act of defiance as much as devotion, because to stop would be to accept that men are less than elves, and that the Stormcloaks will never accept.</ideoDescription>
        <deityPresets>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Akatosh</name><type>Dragon God of Time and chief of the Divines</type></nameType>
                <gender>Male</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityAkatosh</iconPath>
            </li>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Arkay</name><type>God of the Cycle of Life and Death</type></nameType>
                <gender>Male</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityArkay</iconPath>
            </li>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Dibella</name><type>Goddess of Beauty and Love</type></nameType>
                <gender>Female</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityDibella</iconPath>
            </li>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Julianos</name><type>God of Wisdom and Logic</type></nameType>
                <gender>Male</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityJulianos</iconPath>
            </li>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Kynareth</name><type>Goddess of the Heavens and Wind</type></nameType>
                <gender>Female</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityKynareth</iconPath>
            </li>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Mara</name><type>Goddess of Love and Compassion</type></nameType>
                <gender>Female</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityMara</iconPath>
            </li>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Stendarr</name><type>God of Mercy and Justice</type></nameType>
                <gender>Male</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityStendarr</iconPath>
            </li>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Zenithar</name><type>God of Work and Commerce</type></nameType>
                <gender>Male</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityZenithar</iconPath>
            </li>
            <li>
                <nameType><name>Talos</name><type>God of Man and Governance</type></nameType>
                <gender>Male</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/ESCP_DeityTalos</iconPath>
            </li>
        </deityPresets>
        <styles>
            <li>ESCP_Style_Nord</li>
        </styles>
        <forcedMemes>
            <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Structure_Ideological</li>
            <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">ESCP_Meme_NineDivines</li>
        </forcedMemes>
        <requiredPreceptsOnly>true</requiredPreceptsOnly>

        <xenotypeSet>
            <xenotypeChances>
                <Neanderthal MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0</Neanderthal>
                <Hussar MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0</Hussar>
                <Pigskin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0</Pigskin>
                <Yttakin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0</Yttakin>
                <Genie MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0</Genie>
                <Dirtmole MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0</Dirtmole>
                <Highmate MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0</Highmate>
            </xenotypeChances>
        </xenotypeSet>

        <backstoryFilters>
            <li>
                <categories>
                    <li>ESCP_Backstory_Nord_Child</li>
                    <li>ESCP_Backstory_Stormcloak_Child</li>
                    <li>ESCP_Backstory_Nord_Military</li>
                    <li>ESCP_Backstory_Stormcloak_Military</li>
                    <li>ESCP_Backstory_Stormcloak_Citizen</li>
                </categories>
                <commonality>0.95</commonality>
            </li>
        </backstoryFilters>

        <allowedArrivalTemperatureRange>-60~40</allowedArrivalTemperatureRange>
        <maxPawnCostPerTotalPointsCurve>
            <points>
                <li>(0, 35)</li>
                <li>(70, 50)</li>
                <li>(700, 100)</li>
                <li>(1300, 150)</li>
                <li>(100000, 10000)</li>
            </points>
        </maxPawnCostPerTotalPointsCurve>

        <pawnGroupMakers>
            <li>
                <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
                <options>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Soldier>14</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Soldier>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Archer>5</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Archer>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Berserker>6</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Berserker>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Officer>2</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Officer>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Commander>1</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Commander>
                </options>
            </li>
            <li>
                <kindDef>Peaceful</kindDef>
                <options>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Citizen>20</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Citizen>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Nord_Merchant>10</ESCP_Pawnkind_Nord_Merchant>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Nord_Skald>5</ESCP_Pawnkind_Nord_Skald>
                </options>
            </li>
            <li>
                <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
                <options>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Citizen>8</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Citizen>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Soldier>14</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Soldier>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Archer>6</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Archer>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Berserker>5</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Berserker>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Officer>3</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Officer>
                    <ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Commander>1</ESCP_Pawnkind_Stormcloak_Commander>
                </options>
            </li>
        </pawnGroupMakers>
        <settlementTexturePath>World/WorldObjects/DefaultSettlement</settlementTexturePath>

        <modExtensions Inherit="False">
            <li Class="ESCP_RaceTools.FactionProperties">
                <factionTags>
                    <li>ESCP_TalosWorship</li>
                </factionTags>
            </li>
            <li Class="ESCP.Factions.FactionExtension_FlavorOverride">
                <newLabel>Stormcloak Rebellion</newLabel>
            </li>
            <li Class="ESCP.Factions.FactionExtension_PermanentlyHostileTo">
                <hostileFactionDefs>
                    <li>ESCP_Faction_Kingdom_of_Skyrim</li>
                </hostileFactionDefs>
            </li>
            <li Class="ESCP.Factions.FactionExtension_BannedArrivalModes">
                <arrivalModes>
                    <li>EdgeDrop</li>
                    <li>EdgeDropGroups</li>
                    <li>CenterDrop</li>
                    <li>RandomDrop</li>
                </arrivalModes>
            </li>
        </modExtensions>
    </FactionDef>

</Defs>
